Leaderboard order is scrambled. Save /workspace/leaderboard.js:

function topScores(scores, n) {
  return scores.sort().reverse().slice(0, n);
}
module.exports = { topScores };

Array.prototype.sort without a comparator sorts numbers as strings, and it also mutates the caller's array. Write leaderboard.test.js (node:test) first: topScores([5, 100, 9, 22], 2) must be [100, 22], and after the call the original input array must still be [5, 100, 9, 22]. Run node --test, see both assertions fail, then fix (numeric comparator, copy before sorting). Add a tie-handling test and one with negative scores. Green before you stop.

